# The tally must equal the number of highlights on screen.
#
# The highlight is drawn per RENDERED line — after markdown normalization and
# inline-marker parsing — while the obvious thing to count is the stored text.
# Those differ: "**6 failures**" stores ten characters around the phrase and
# paints six, and a fenced code block is rendered by a different path that
# carries no highlight at all. Counting the stored text therefore promised
# matches that could never be shown.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t4"],"active_tab":"t4","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_FIND_DEMO=prorate

# "prorate" appears in this thread — but only inside a fenced code block, which
# has no highlight path. Not paintable, so not counted.
expect_text "no matches"
